1:["$","main",null,{"className":"site article-page","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"article-frame","children":[["$","$La",null,{"className":"desktop-brand","href":"/","children":"Thinkinghaus"}],["$","article",null,{"className":"article-column","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"article-header","children":[["$","h1",null,{"children":"The silent type"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"August 6, 2026"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"2 minutes"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"article-body","children":[[["$","p","0-Untitled Sans began as an attempt to make another typeface plainer.",{"children":"Untitled Sans began as an attempt to make another typeface plainer."}],["$","p","1-Kris Sowersby removed some of its more noticeable details, got a little lost and put the project away, returned to it several years later, and nearly threw it out. Reading about the Super Normal project eventually helped him understand why a deliberately ordinary typeface might be worth finishing.",{"children":"Kris Sowersby removed some of its more noticeable details, got a little lost and put the project away, returned to it several years later, and nearly threw it out. Reading about the Super Normal project eventually helped him understand why a deliberately ordinary typeface might be worth finishing."}],["$","p","2-I like that the reasoning came later. Design processes are often written up as though every decision followed neatly from the one before it. Mine rarely work that way. I try things. I change my mind. I forget why I started. Occasionally I end up with something useful.",{"children":"I like that the reasoning came later. Design processes are often written up as though every decision followed neatly from the one before it. Mine rarely work that way. I try things. I change my mind. I forget why I started. Occasionally I end up with something useful."}],["$","p","3-Sowersby describes removing traces of his own recognizable style from the letters. His goal wasn’t to make the typeface distinctive. It was to make something that could be successful without bringing a ton of baggage along with it.",{"children":"Sowersby describes removing traces of his own recognizable style from the letters. His goal wasn’t to make the typeface distinctive. It was to make something that could be successful without bringing a ton of baggage along with it."}],["$","p","4-In design, as in life, that is extremely difficult to pull off. Designers are generally encouraged to—and take delight in—making things memorable. A plain typeface can feel like a missed opportunity. But most of the time I don’t need the type to be the most interesting thing on the page. I need it to help me read.",{"children":"In design, as in life, that is extremely difficult to pull off. Designers are generally encouraged to—and take delight in—making things memorable. A plain typeface can feel like a missed opportunity. But most of the time I don’t need the type to be the most interesting thing on the page. I need it to help me read."}],["$","p","5-That’s probably why Untitled Sans feels right for both my portfolio site and for this site. My work and my writing can wander around and follow unusual ideas. The letters stay put.",{"children":"That’s probably why Untitled Sans feels right for both my portfolio site and for this site. My work and my writing can wander around and follow unusual ideas. The letters stay put."}],["$","p","6-Untitled Sans is very much a designed artifact. Its plainness is the result of a mountain of small, thoughtful, beautiful choices. It just doesn’t ask me to admire and praise those choices every time I read a paragraph.",{"children":"Untitled Sans is very much a designed artifact. Its plainness is the result of a mountain of small, thoughtful, beautiful choices. It just doesn’t ask me to admire and praise those choices every time I read a paragraph."}],"$Lb"],"$Lc"]}],"$Ld"]}]]}]}]
b:["$","p","7-There is something deeply appealing to me about creating something that works so incredibly well without constantly advertising how much work went into it. Creating something that knows how to be quiet.",{"children":"There is something deeply appealing to me about creating something that works so incredibly well without constantly advertising how much work went into it. Creating something that knows how to be quiet."}]
